<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#zugewandter-ort">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zugewandter Ort</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Associate of the Swiss Confederacy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A Zugewandter Ort (associated place) was a territory allied with the Old Swiss Confederacy without being a full member canton. Associates such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valais">Valais</a>, the Three Leagues of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/graubunden">Grisons</a>, the abbey and city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-gallen">St. Gallen</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> were linked to some or all of the cantons by treaties of alliance, but had no full vote in the federal Diet. Most became cantons after the Napoleonic period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zugewandter-ort.jpg" alt="Zugewandter Ort" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marco Zanoli (sidonius 19:13, 3 May 2007 (UTC)) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karte_Zugewandte_Orte.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
